From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] toolbutton: install the accelerator once the window has an application

activityinstance builds the Activity - toolbar and all - and only then
calls app.add_window(activity). So when a ToolButton's notify::root
fires, root.get_application() is still None, _add_accelerator() returns
early, and nothing ever retries: no Gio action is created and the
accelerator is bound to nothing for the life of the process.

ToggleToolButton already has the missing half - it connects "map" and
re-runs _add_accelerator there, by which time add_window() has happened.
ToolButton was never given the same retry, so Sugar's plain tool button
accelerators (Stop's <Ctrl>Q, Copy's <Ctrl>C, Paste's <Ctrl>V, and every
accelerator an Activity sets on a ToolButton) are dead in the GTK4 port.

Give ToolButton the same map retry, and remember the installed action so
a repeated map replaces it instead of leaking a new one, which is what
ToggleToolButton does.

--- a/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbutton.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/graphics/toolbutton.py
@@ -78,6 +78,11 @@
     # GTK4: Use application shortcuts instead of AccelGroup
     app = root.get_application() if hasattr(root, "get_application") else None
     if app and hasattr(app, "set_accels_for_action"):
+        # Replace anything installed on an earlier attempt.
+        previous = getattr(tool_button, "_accel_action_name", None)
+        if previous:
+            app.remove_action(previous)
+
         # Create a unique action name for this button
         action_name = f"toolbutton.{id(tool_button)}"
 
@@ -90,11 +95,13 @@
             app.set_accels_for_action(
                 f"app.{action_name}", [tool_button.props.accelerator]
             )
+            tool_button._accel_action_name = action_name
         elif hasattr(root, "add_action"):
             root.add_action(action)
             app.set_accels_for_action(
                 f"win.{action_name}", [tool_button.props.accelerator]
             )
+            tool_button._accel_action_name = action_name
 
 
 def _hierarchy_changed_cb(tool_button):
@@ -108,6 +115,12 @@
         tool_button.connect(
             "notify::root", lambda *args: _hierarchy_changed_cb(tool_button)
         )
+        # activityinstance builds the toolbar, then hands the window to the
+        # Gtk.Application, so notify::root fires while get_application() is
+        # still None and the action is never installed. ToggleToolButton
+        # already retries on map; ToolButton did not, which left every
+        # Sugar tool button accelerator dead.
+        tool_button.connect("map", lambda *args: _add_accelerator(tool_button))
 
 
 class ToolButton(Gtk.Button):
